					<description><![CDATA[<p>WWE Raw ResultsNovember 9, 2026Greenville, South Carolina (Bon Secours Wellness Arena)Commentary: Joe Tessitore and Wade BarrettResults by: Mike&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-raw-results/397068-live-wwe-raw-results-november-9-2026-greenville/">WWE Raw Results &#8211; 11/9/26 (Fallout from Crown Jewel, Cody Rhodes to appear)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<figure class="wp-block-image is-resized"><img decoding="async" width="207" height="112" src="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/image-21.png" alt="" class="wp-image-375213" style="aspect-ratio:1.8482142857142858;width:207px;height:auto"/></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>WWE Raw Results<br>November 9, 2026<br>Greenville, South Carolina (Bon Secours Wellness Arena)<br>Commentary: Joe Tessitore and Wade Barrett<br>Results by: Mike Tedesco of Wrestleview.com</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;Then. Now. Forever. Together.&#8221; The WWE video leads us into the show.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The WWE Drone flies around the exterior of the Bon Secours Wellness Arena.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Raw Open:</strong> Highlights from <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/396823-wwe-crown-jewel-results-11-7-26-mens-and-womens-crown-jewel-championships-and-more/">this past Saturday&#8217;s WWE Crown Jewel</a> event are shown.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Pre-Show Arrivals</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">World Heavyweight Champion Roman Reigns, Jade Cargill, WWE Women&#8217;s Tag Team Champions B-Fab and Michin, WWE Intercontinental Champion &#8220;All Ego&#8221; Ethan Page, and &#8220;The American Nightmare&#8221; Cody Rhodes are shown arriving for WWE Raw.</p>



<h3 id="world-tag-team-champions-jevon-evans-and-penta-kick-off-wwe-raw" class="wp-block-heading">World Tag Team Champions Je&#8217;Von Evans and Penta kick off WWE Raw</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>World Tag Team Champions Je&#8217;Von Evans and Penta</strong> make their entrance to the ring. They defeated Bron Breakker and Austin Theory to win the World Tag Team Championship this past Saturday at WWE Crown Jewel. Penta also holds the Money in the Bank briefcase. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Penta and Evans get the crowd going. Penta thanks the crowd and says they love them. Penta shouts that he and Evans are the new World Tag Team Champions. Evans apologizes and says he doesn&#8217;t mean to be selfish, but this is his first WWE Title of his career. If you&#8217;re proud or excited for the Young OG or Penta, they can say, &#8220;YURR.&#8221; The crowd says it lightly, so Evans gets them to do it again. A &#8220;You Deserve It&#8221; chant picks up. Penta says they are standing here as the new champions. The most important thing is that Penta has zero miedo. Penta and Evans embrace in the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">All of a sudden, <strong>Bron Breakker</strong> viciously hits Penta with a Spear! Breakker then hits a military press gutbuster on Evans before tossing him out of the ring. The crowd boos Breakker. Breakker says there is one man he has to fight, and he&#8217;s not leaving until they do. Breakker calls Oba Femi out. The crowd starts to chant for Femi.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>&#8220;The Ruler&#8221; Oba Femi</strong> makes his entrance to a great ovation, and he&#8217;s dressed to compete! Femi charges into the ring, attacks Breakker, and hits him with a clothesline over the top rope! Femi mentions that Breakker said tonight in Greenville. Breakker has got it!</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Simple opener with Penta and Je&#39;Von Evans celebrating before Bron Breakker attacked them. <br><br>The bigger news is that Bron Breakker is taking on Oba Femi right now! A match that honestly should be held off for an eventual PLE main event far down the line is happening on <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWERaw?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWERaw</a>.</p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119962860529008988?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 10, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<h3 id="bron-breakker-vs-the-ruler-oba-femi" class="wp-block-heading">Bron Breakker vs. &#8220;The Ruler&#8221; Oba Femi</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Referee:</strong> Rod Zapata</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The bell rings, and Breakker quickly attacks Femi before shouldering him in the midsection in the corner. Femi fights back and whips him hard into the opposite corner before connecting with a clothesline. Femi pulls him up, but Breakker powers him into the corner and shoulders him in the midsection. The referee backs Breakker up, and Femi connects with a STIFF straight right hand to the jaw. Femi scoops Breakker up and hits snake eyes. Femi elbows Breakker in the head and wrenches his arm. Femi shoulders him down before scooping him back up. Breakker slides off, ducks a pair of clotheslines, and hits a big clothesline to take The Ruler down. <strong>Logan Paul</strong>, <strong>Austin Theory</strong>, and <strong>Maxxine Dupri</strong> are at ringside. Breakker has Femi cornered and is attacking him. Femi reverses a whip and hits an Irish Curse Backbreaker. Femi mounts Breakker and punches him. Femi hits Breakker with a shoulderbreaker. Breakker gets out of the ring to recover.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Femi exits the ring, and Breakker tackles him into the ring apron. Femi fires back by sending Breakker into the ring post. Femi goes for a running back elbow, but Breakker drives him into the ring post! Breakker bounces Femi off the commentary table and goes to the apron. Breakker dives off with a clothesline over the table! Joe Tessitore way oversells the call.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Picture-in-Picture Commercial Break:</strong> After a few moments taken to recover, Breakker attacks Femi before getting him into the ring. Breakker punches him in the corner and taunts the crowd. Breakker whips Femi hard into the corner shoulder-first. Breakker hits Femi with a vertical suplex for a two-count. Breakker applies a front facelock. Femi fights up to his feet and applies a bear hug, but Breakker fights out. Femi whips Breakker into the corner and hits a running back elbow. Femi tries again, but Breakker moves. Breakker punches Femi and taunts the crowd.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the break, Breakker mocks Femi&#8217;s strut. Breakker goes for a vertical suplex, but Femi blocks it. Breakker fights through and hits Femi with a vertical suplex for a two-count. Breakker sets up for another suplex, but Femi fires back with a vertical release suplex.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After a moment to recover, Femi hits Breakker with a pop-up uppercut. Femi hits a pair of running back elbows in the corner before dropping Breakker with a leaping back elbow. Breakker rolls out of the ring, so Femi follows him out and hits a leaping back elbow over the commentary table! Femi stands on the table and holds his arm in pain. Femi gets Breakker into the ring. Breakker distracts the referee as Theory grabs Femi. Femi easily kicks Theory away and gets into the ring. Breakker goes for a Spear, but Femi drives him into the ring post. Femi hits a massive Chokeslam and covers. 1&#8230; 2&#8230; Breakker kicks out.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Femi gets to his feet and holds his injured shoulder as he signals for another Chokeslam. Breakker gets out, so Femi big boots him. Breakker boots him back, but Femi hits a running uppercut. Breakker hits the ropes and hits Femi with a Torpedo Spear! 1&#8230; 2&#8230; Femi kicks out. The referee checks on Femi as Logan Paul slides a pair of brass knuckles to Breakker. Breakker puts them on. Femi ducks a loaded right hand and hits a release slam on Breakker. Paul quickly jumps onto the apron to distract the referee. Femi goes for the Fall from Grace, but Breakker punches him in the forehead with the brass knuckles! Femi collapses. Breakker pulls his straps down and hits the ropes for a Torpedo Spear, but Femi stuns him with a Fall from Grace! Theory and Paul quickly get into the ring and double-team Femi.</p>



<h3 id="winner-by-disqualification-the-ruler-oba-femi" class="wp-block-heading">Winner by Disqualification: &#8220;The Ruler&#8221; Oba Femi</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>World Tag Team Champions Penta and Je&#8217;Von Evans</strong> run down for the save, but The Vision quickly escapes before any contact is made.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Oba Femi vs. Bron Breakker had the exact same ending as the <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/SNME?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#SNME</a> match. I think the biggest shocker of this entire thing was how little of a deal this felt. These two should not be fighting often and certainly not for free. What a mishandling of this feud. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWERaw?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWERaw</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119969094036590959?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 10, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Parking Lot Interview</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jackie Redmond is in the parking lot with IYO SKY. Sky&#8217;s partner is a mystery. Sky says this secret is a big advantage for her, so she won&#8217;t say who it is. Sky is excited to see the faces of The Judgment Day when her partner is revealed.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Replay:</strong> <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/396393-wwe-raw-results-11-2-26-special-early-start-time-crown-jewel-go-home-show-john-cena-appears-roman-reigns-title-match/">Last week on Raw</a>, &#8220;All Ego&#8221; Ethan Page defeated Chad Gable to win the WWE Intercontinental Championship.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Backstage Photo Shoot</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">WWE Intercontinental Champion Ethan Page is taking professional photos with several models. We&#8217;ll hear from him next.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Buy a spot for your name on the WWE canvas at Survivor Series for $10,000, or something like that.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Parking Lot Segment</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jaida Parker knocks on a van, and out steps 946.</p>



<h3 id="wwe-intercontinental-champion-ethan-page-addresses-his-victory" class="wp-block-heading">WWE Intercontinental Champion Ethan Page addresses his victory</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>WWE Intercontinental Champion &#8220;All Ego&#8221; Ethan Page</strong> heads to the ring with his entourage of women. Page says it was inevitable. Last week, he beat a guy on the run of his life to win the Intercontinental Championship. Chad Gable was great, but he wasn&#8217;t a great champion. Gable was just a man who trained hard, lost his confidence and identity, went to Mexico to embark on a redemption tour, and decided to bring his wife and kids along. Now the Intercontinental Championship is held by a real man. Page doesn&#8217;t need to bring his wife on the road because he&#8217;s got four potential wives. Maybe he&#8217;ll bring someone else&#8217;s wife. The most important thing is the title is held by &#8220;All Ego&#8221; Ethan Page.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Chad Gable</strong> interrupts, dressed to compete. Page tells his entourage to leave so he can handle this business. Gable says he&#8217;s out here to congratulate Page because he beat him fair and square. A year ago, this presentation would have really gotten under his skin, but Gable isn&#8217;t letting it bother him. What bothers him is Page talking about his family. Even if Gable handled this with all the dignity in the world, it doesn&#8217;t change the fact that Page is &#8220;just an asshole.&#8221; An &#8220;a&#8211;hole&#8221; chant picks up.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Big Cass&#8217; music hits</strong>. Cass says we can all see where this is going. Cass wants Page to face facts. If it weren&#8217;t for Cass, Page wouldn&#8217;t be the Intercontinental Champion. Cass gets into the ring. If anybody deserves the first shot at the title, it&#8217;s not Gable. It&#8217;s Cass.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>AAA World Cruiserweight Champion Rey Fénix </strong>interrupts. The last time he was on Raw, he beat Ethan Page. The first person to get the shot has to be him. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fénix, Cass, and Gable argue. Page says they&#8217;re making fantastic points. Gable is an Olympian and more dialed in than anyone he&#8217;s met in wrestling, but the Intercontinental Championship is still his ceiling. Fénix is a top star, just not here. As for Cass, he is tall. They make great points, but Page isn&#8217;t a matchmaker. They can debate amongst themselves and run it up the ladder before letting him know who gets the first match.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Raw General Manager Adam Pearce</strong> walks out to the stage and cannot believe he agrees with Ethan Page. They do need a No. 1 Contender, and all three have a claim at it. Pearce makes a Triple Threat No. 1 Contender&#8217;s Match right now. It is official!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<h3 id="no-1-contenders-matchtriple-threat-matchchad-gable-vs-big-cass-vs-aaa-world-cruiserweight-champion-rey-fenix" class="wp-block-heading"><strong>No. 1 Contender&#8217;s Match</strong><br><em>Triple Threat Match</em><br>Chad Gable vs. Big Cass vs. AAA World Cruiserweight Champion Rey Fénix</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Referee:</strong> Eddie Orengo</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">WWE Intercontinental Champion &#8220;All Ego&#8221; Ethan Page will be on commentary for this match.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We join this match in progress to see Cass run over Fénix and Gable with a double clothesline. Cass goes back and forth, avalanching them in the corner. Fénix sidesteps Cass and kicks away at him. Fénix and Gable then hit Cass with stereo superkicks, knocking him out of the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Gable and Fénix shake hands before exchanging punches and kicks. Fénix goes for a powerbomb, but Gable gets out. Gable attempts one, but Fénix slips out. Fénix counters an Olympic Slam into an arm drag. Fénix charges Gable in the corner, but Gable hits an overhead belly-to-belly suplex into the turnbuckles for a two-count. Gable goes to the top rope for a moonsault, but he lands on his feet when Fénix moves. Fénix immediately hits Gable with a beautiful cutter for a near fall. Fénix sizes Gable up and goes for a running superkick, but Gable counters with an Ankle Lock. Fénix twists and kicks Gable in the face, but Gable turns him over and keeps the Ankle Lock applied. Fénix twists to get Gable out of the ring. Cass then hits Gable with a Boss Man Slam on the floor! Fénix goes for a suicide dive on Cass, but Cass catches him. Fénix avoids a Chokeslam on the apron, but Cass quickly big boots him down!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cass grabs Gable. Gable fights back, but Cass drives him into the barricade. Cass then Chokeslams Gable over the timekeeper&#8217;s barricade onto a stagehand! Joe Tessitore once again oversells the call going into the commercial break.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the break, Gable hits Fénix with a pair of German Suplexes. Cass runs up, but Gable sidesteps and goes for a German Suplex. Cass fights it, so Fénix hits Cass with a lungblower. Gable hits Cass with an Angle Slam for a near fall. Gable applies an Ankle Lock to Cass, but he releases to avoid a dive from Fénix. Fénix goes for a handspring back elbow, but Gable takes him down and locks in the Ankle Lock. Fénix counters into a roll-up for a two-count. Cass big boots Gable. Fénix kicks away at Cass. Cass blocks a superkick, but Fénix gets him tied up in the ropes and stuns him with a kick to the skull. Fénix runs on the top rope for the Adios, Amigo! Fénix goes to the top rope, but Gable runs Cass into him and hits the Chaos Theory German Suplex.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Gable&#8217;s neck injury gets reaggravated, and he holds his arm in pain. Fénix stuns Gable with an Adios, Amigo. Cass quickly crotches Fénix on the top rope and hits Gable with a Chokeslam. 1&#8230; 2&#8230; Fénix breaks it up with a Frog Splash! Fénix then pins Gable for the win!</p>



<h3 id="winner-by-pinfall-aaa-world-cruiserweight-champion-rey-fenix" class="wp-block-heading">Winner by Pinfall: AAA World Cruiserweight Champion Rey Fénix</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">All of a sudden, <strong>946</strong> charges in through the crowd and viciously attacks Fénix and Gable! Royce Keys watches on as Carmelo Hayes, Bronco Nima, Lucien Price, and Cruz Montana take it to all three men in the ring. Gable, Fénix, and Cass are all getting it. Keys calmly brings a chair into the ring and sits down. Montana wipes out Fénix with a discus lariat. Nima and Price hit Cass with a double-team Samoan Drop.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Keys takes a microphone and says, &#8220;One by one by one by one.&#8221; Keys holds up a finger to call out Roman Reigns. Keys says this could be Reigns&#8217; family unless he brings his ass out here tonight to acknowledge him. The 946 is fired up.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Strong Triple Threat match with some good action. I like that they&#39;re starting to get behind Rey Fénix from a booking perspective. The run-in by 946 was well done and a good reminder that ain&#39;t nobody safe. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWERaw?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWERaw</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119978804328464663?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 10, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Replay:</strong> Moments ago, The 946 attacked Rey Fénix, Big Cass, and Chad Gable. Royce Keys then called out Roman Reigns.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Later tonight, World Heavyweight Champion Roman Reigns will go face-to-face with Royce Keys.</p>



<h3 id="cody-rhodes-addresses-punting-randy-orton-in-the-head" class="wp-block-heading">Cody Rhodes addresses punting Randy Orton in the head</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Replay:</strong> <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/396823-wwe-crown-jewel-results-11-7-26-mens-and-womens-crown-jewel-championships-and-more/">This past Saturday at WWE Crown Jewel</a>, Cody Rhodes defeated Randy Orton in a Last Man Standing match after punting his former mentor in the skull.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;Wrestling has more than one royal family.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>&#8220;The American Nightmare&#8221; Cody Rhodes</strong> heads to the ring. Rhodes will head up Team USA against Team Mexico, led by Rey Mysterio, at Survivor Series.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Rhodes asks the crowd what they want to talk about. This past Saturday, he defeated Randy Orton and was the Last Man Standing. Rhodes didn&#8217;t need to Punt him to win, but he did. Everyone has been asking him how it felt. Rhodes says he liked it, but then said he&#8217;d be lying if he said that. Rhodes didn&#8217;t like it&#8230; he LOVED it.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Now that that nasty business is in the rearview mirror, he looks ahead to Survivor Series, where he will lead Team USA against Team Mexico. As the captain of Team USA, he wants to talk captain-to-captain, so he brings out <strong>WWE Hall of Famer Rey Mysterio</strong> to the ring. Mysterio heads to the ring. Mysterio says he wants to put together the best of Mexico against the best of the USA. Mysterio couldn&#8217;t think of a better captain for Team USA than The American Nightmare when they throw down in Houston. They do have the opportunity to choose four other members. That won&#8217;t be easy.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Rhodes says Mysterio has to know this&#8230; he&#8217;s the greatest luchador of all time. Rhodes knows Mysterio plans to put together a banner team for Team Mexico. Rhodes has been in the habit of keeping promises, so he promises to do the same for Team USA.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>&#8220;Dirty&#8221; Dominik Mysterio</strong> and <strong>JD McDonagh</strong> interrupt. Dominik scoffs that his father is the greatest luchador of all time, but Rhodes is forgetting about the King of the Luchadores. Dominik cannot believe that the captain for Team Mexico is his father. Dominik and McDonagh get into the ring. Not only is Rey a deadbeat, but he&#8217;s cheating on his mother with some old hag. With that being said, Dominik doesn&#8217;t want personal issues to get in the way of Rey picking top talent for Team Mexico. Dominik will happily join the team and take over as captain so Rey can go back to AAA where he belongs.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Rey says Dominik might be onto something. Dominik as team captain for Mexico&#8230; he can get his punk ass out of the ring because Rey&#8217;s answer is no. Dominik says Rey has always been an idiot, but Cody Rhodes is a man with vision. Rhodes knows he needs the King of the Luchadores as an asset against Team Mexico. Rhodes needs &#8220;Dirty&#8221; Dominik Mysterio on Team USA. Dominik was born in the United States. The crowd chants, &#8220;NO.&#8221; Rhodes extends his hand, and Dominik shakes it. Rhodes sarcastically says that was an incredible offer, but on behalf of the team he hasn&#8217;t put together yet, the people of Greenville, and the entire United States of America, they&#8217;re going to pass. Dominik is not happy. Who is Rhodes going to get who is better than Dominik?</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>CM Punk&#8217;s music hits!</strong> The Second City Saint makes his way to the ring to a great reception. Punk asks if it&#8217;s great to be alive on a Monday night in Greenville or what? Punk says he&#8217;s taken some big L&#8217;s recently. On the last SmackDown, he was on the bad end of a chain-wrapped fist. What does the Best in the World do? He doesn&#8217;t sulk and cry. He tries to get back into the win column. When Punk hears about a Traditional 5-on-5 Survivor Series match, he gets excited. He could get back into title contention by beating five guys in five weeks, but what if he does it in one night? As much as Punk respects Rey, the apple fell far from the tree (Dominik). Punk is putting his name in the hat for Team USA and gets a USA chant going. Punk says, &#8220;Cody, if you&#8217;ll have me, I&#8217;ll be your huckleberry.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Dominik is incredulous that Rhodes is letting an &#8220;old has-been&#8221; on the team. Dominik deserves to be on the team. McDonagh shoves Punk. Punk takes his jacket off and looks around. Punk kicks McDonagh into the ropes. Rhodes drops down and uppercuts Dominik into the ropes. Rey hits Dominik and McDonagh with a double 619! Punk hits McDonagh with a Go to Sleep, while Rhodes hits Dominik with a Cross Rhodes. Punk and Rhodes shake hands with Rey before raising their arms up.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Fun segment with Rey Mysterio, Cody Rhodes, and CM Punk getting the better of Dominik Mysterio and JD McDonagh. I love a good Traditional Survivor Series match. It&#39;s been a while! <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWERaw?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWERaw</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119984288158659071?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 10, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Survivor Series photo and autograph experience is coming on Survivor Series weekend.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Replay:</strong> <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/396393-wwe-raw-results-11-2-26-special-early-start-time-crown-jewel-go-home-show-john-cena-appears-roman-reigns-title-match/">Last week on Raw</a>, Bayley confronted Jade Cargill, B-Fab, and Michin before they attacked her. On <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/396519-wwe-smackdown-results-11-6-26-final-show-before-crown-jewel-tag-title-match-no-holds-barred/">SmackDown</a>, Charlotte Flair stopped Cargill from attacking Bayley. Fatal Influence tried to get involved, but Bayley, Tatum Paxley, Flair, and Alexa Bliss fought them off.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bayley heads to the ring to battle Michin next.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<h3 id="bayley-vs-wwe-womens-tag-team-champion-michin" class="wp-block-heading">Bayley vs. WWE Women&#8217;s Tag Team Champion Michin</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Referee:</strong> Shawn Bennett</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bayley takes it to Michin at the start of the match, but Michin fires back by raking her eyes and suplexing her for a two-count. Michin attacks Bayley and heads to the top rope. Bayley cuts her off, but Michin kicks her in the knee, knocking her down. Michin connects with a missile dropkick, knocking Bayley out of the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the break, Bayley snaps Michin off the middle rope for a two-count. Bayley sets up for a Rose Plant, but Michin counters into a roll-up for a two-count. Michin quickly drives Bayley into the turnbuckles and hits a German Suplex with a bridge for a near fall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bayley gets up and forearms away at Michin. Michin blocks a kick and hits a sit-out powerbomb for a two-count. Michin boots Bayley in the head several times and hits the ropes, but Bayley takes her down with a crossface. Michin twists out and goes for a powerbomb, but Bayley counters with a back body drop. Bayley connects with the Bayley-to-Belly for a near fall. Bayley goes for the Rose Plant again, but Michin fights out. Michin goes for Eat Defeat, but Bayley blocks it and applies a single-leg crab. Michin twists out and kicks her away. Michin then drops her with Eat Defeat. Michin takes a moment to recover before charging, but Bayley sidesteps her, causing her to hit the ring post. Bayley hits a sunset flip bomb into the turnbuckles for a two-count. Bayley heads to the top rope, but Michin rolls to the apron. Michin pulls Bayley&#8217;s ribs into the turnbuckle bracket and goes to the top rope, but Bayley slams her down. Bayley goes to the top rope for a flying elbow drop, picking up the win.</p>



<h3 id="winner-by-pinfall-bayley" class="wp-block-heading">Winner by Pinfall: Bayley</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>B-Fab</strong> and <strong>Jade Cargill</strong> storm down to the ring and attack Bayley. They triple-team Bayley. <strong>Charlotte Flair</strong> heads to the ring with <strong>Tatum Paxley</strong> and <strong>Alexa Bliss</strong>. <strong>Fatal Influence </strong>appears and attacks them outside the ring. Jacy Jayne rolls an unconscious Flair into the ring. Cargill hits Flair with Jaded. Jayne gets in the ring with Fatal Influence and shakes hands with Cargill.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Just a match with Bayley and Michin. There was nothing wrong with it, but the crowd was asleep for it. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWERaw?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWERaw</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119987560260747757?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 10, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Backstage Segment</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>World Tag Team Champion Penta</strong> is backstage, holding his ribs. <strong>Rey Mysterio</strong> walks over to check on him and congratulate him on the victory at WWE Crown Jewel. Mysterio says Penta is the Tag Team Champion and has the Money in the Bank briefcase&#8230; he doesn&#8217;t want to add more stress to Penta. Cody Rhodes announced CM Punk as part of Team USA. Team Mexico wouldn&#8217;t be complete without Penta. Penta says Mexico gave him everything, <strong>so he&#8217;ll fight for Mexico</strong>. Penta is in. Penta and Mysterio embrace.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Women&#8217;s World Champion Liv Morgan leads Roxanne Perez and WWE Women&#8217;s Intercontinental Champion Raquel Rodriguez to the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">IYO SKY makes her entrance. She&#8217;s followed by her mystery partner, <strong>Becky Lynch</strong>.</p>



<h3 id="tag-team-matchthe-judgment-day-roxanne-perez-and-wwe-womens-intercontinental-champion-raquel-rodriguez-w-womens-world-champion-liv-morgan-vs-iyo-sky-and-the-man-becky-l" class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Tag Team Match</strong><br>The Judgment Day (Roxanne Perez and WWE Women&#8217;s Intercontinental Champion Raquel Rodriguez) w/ Women&#8217;s World Champion Liv Morgan vs. IYO SKY and &#8220;The Man&#8221; Becky Lynch</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Referee:</strong> Jessika Carr</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Refresh for the latest results.</em></p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 id="quick-match-results" class="wp-block-heading">Quick Match Results</h3>



<p class="cnvs-block-core-paragraph-1794274532645 wp-block-paragraph">&#8212; &#8220;The Ruler&#8221; Oba Femi def. Bron Breakker via DQ<br>&#8212; AAA World Cruiserweight Champion Rey Fénix def. Chad Gable* and Big Cass in a No. 1 Contender&#8217;s Triple Threat Match<br>&#8212; Bayley def. WWE Women&#8217;s Tag Team Champion Michin</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-raw-results/397068-live-wwe-raw-results-november-9-2026-greenville/">WWE Raw Results &#8211; 11/9/26 (Fallout from Crown Jewel, Cody Rhodes to appear)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-raw-results/397068-live-wwe-raw-results-november-9-2026-greenville/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Andrade El Idolo reveals pitch made prior to WWE departure</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397064-andrade-el-idolo-reveals-pitch-made-prior-to-wwe-departure/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397064-andrade-el-idolo-reveals-pitch-made-prior-to-wwe-departure/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 23:46:26 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Andrade El Idolo]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[contract dispute]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[creative pitch]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397064</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>During an interview on Talk is Jericho, Andrade El Idolo spoke on the circumstances surrounding his departure from&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397064-andrade-el-idolo-reveals-pitch-made-prior-to-wwe-departure/">Andrade El Idolo reveals pitch made prior to WWE departure</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">During an interview on <a href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/0o67n0BBrICiCTwx5mFE9q">Talk is Jericho</a>, Andrade El Idolo spoke on the circumstances surrounding his departure from WWE in 2025.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">El Idolo explained that his return to the company the prior year was partly motivated by then-wife Charlotte Flair, wanting to be around to support her during her recovery from knee injury, but the subsequent divorce and certain creative pitches from WWE led to his decision to leave:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I went back to WWE to work with my ex-wife, and now that I’m divorced I felt a little weird. I wasn’t feeling at home or comfy. The story they gave, it wasn’t a good or specific good story or direction. Later, they wanted to send me to AAA. ‘Hey Andrade, It’s a good opportunity.’ I moved here to work with WWE.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I know AAA and respect AAA, I’ve respect for all the other companies but WWE is worldwide, and AAA is just in Mexico. People in Mexico know me. I wanted people to know me around the world, like in Australia, Arabia, Europe, and other countries where WWE have, where you can see on TV or Netflix or whatever. But it’s like back to Mexico and this for me like I prefer working in AEW and enjoy it.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I made my name in Mexico so why go back to Mexico? I wanted to work in WWE with the top guys. It’s little things like no, I didn’t feel good…We were talking, I didn’t feel comfortable here. We talked and they gave me my release.</p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Legal complications led to a disruption of his televised appearances for AEW, which finally came to an end after El Idolo worked with WWE to resolve issues surrounding a one-year non-compete clause.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Source: <a href="https://www.f4wonline.com/news/wwe/aew-star-walked-away-from-wwe-after-they-revealed-plans-for-him-in-aaa/">F4WOnline</a></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397064-andrade-el-idolo-reveals-pitch-made-prior-to-wwe-departure/">Andrade El Idolo reveals pitch made prior to WWE departure</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397064-andrade-el-idolo-reveals-pitch-made-prior-to-wwe-departure/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Report: Update on scrapped WWE Crown Jewel match</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397061-report-update-on-scrapped-wwe-crown-jewel-match/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397061-report-update-on-scrapped-wwe-crown-jewel-match/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 21:54:25 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Crown Jewel]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Premium Live Event]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Riyadh]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Saudi Arabia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397061</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>New details have emerged on the decision to scrap a planned match at WWE Crown Jewel on 11/7.&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397061-report-update-on-scrapped-wwe-crown-jewel-match/">Report: Update on scrapped WWE Crown Jewel match</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">New details have emerged on the decision to scrap a planned match at WWE Crown Jewel on 11/7.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A new report from <a href="https://www.f4wonline.com/news/wwe/subscriber-exclusive-wwe-star-opted-not-to-go-to-saudi-arabia-for-crown-jewel/">F4WOnline</a> has revealed that a bout between Gunther and Finn Balor was ultimately dropped from the premium live event&#8217;s lineup because Gunther decided against traveling to Saudi Arabia.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Multiple WWE sources reportedly confirmed the former World Heavyweight Champion&#8217;s decision was responsible for the change, with one source indicating that the situation went back and forth behind the scenes leading to the continued angles on television despite the bout&#8217;s uncertainty.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It was also noted that Balor had reservations about making the trip, though the belief internally is that he would have traveled had Gunther agreed to participate.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The situation is noteworthy given the perception among WWE talent that declining to work the events in Saudi Arabia was no longer an option.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397061-report-update-on-scrapped-wwe-crown-jewel-match/">Report: Update on scrapped WWE Crown Jewel match</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397061-report-update-on-scrapped-wwe-crown-jewel-match/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Former WWE talent confirms departure from MLW</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397054-former-wwe-talent-confirms-departure-from-mlw/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397054-former-wwe-talent-confirms-departure-from-mlw/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 19:48:29 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[departure]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Dijak]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[MLW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397054</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>39-year-old Dijak (former WWE talent Dominik Dijakovic) has confirmed reports he has departed MLW and is a free&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397054-former-wwe-talent-confirms-departure-from-mlw/">Former WWE talent confirms departure from MLW</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">39-year-old Dijak (former WWE talent Dominik Dijakovic) has confirmed reports he has departed MLW and is a free agent, following his contract expiring. He was also known as T-Bar during his time in WWE when he was part of the Retribution faction from 2020-2022. Prior to the main roster, he spent 2017 to 2020 on the NXT roster. He left WWE on June 28, 2024 after his contract expired.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In his lengthy post on social media, he had nothing but good things to say about his time in MLW and that a the next presentation of his character will be &#8220;brand new and extraordinarily unique&#8221;, which he also said will debut &#8220;very soon.&#8221; Dijak also noted he is currently taking bookings. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;<em>After much thought and consideration, I have decided that this past weekend was my final appearances for MLW and I will be entering Free Agency moving forward. I am incredibly grateful for my time in MLW, over the past two years I was given an exceptional platform to showcase my abilities as both a singles and tag team wrestler. I was able to capture gold as The Skyscrapers alongside my good friend and tag partner Baron Corbin. I was also able to have incredible matches against Killer Kross, Josh Bishop, Matt Riddle, Krule, Kevin Knight, The Good Brothers, Kenta, and many, many more. Thank you so much to Court Bauer for providing me with such an amazing place to call home.</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>I am so very excited for the next chapter of my career moving forward. I have been wrestling all over the world at an incredibly high level, and I just knew it was time to truly bet on myself. I’m so excited to keep working with incredible independent companies like Progress, Limitless, Juggalo Championship, PW Rebellion, Blood Sweat Tears, and so many other amazing indy companies.</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>2027 is going to be an unbelievably exciting year for me. I am going to be debuting a brand new and extraordinarily unique character presentation very soon, and I’m so excited to share my vision with all of you. I know deep down in my heart that I am currently the best I have ever been in the ring and I can’t wait to continue to showcase my passion and dedication for as many people as possible.</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Thank you all so much for your continued support. It truly means the world to me.</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Now it’s time to Feast Your Eyes on the Dijak Hijack of Free Agency.</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>BookDijak@gmail.com</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>KNOCK KNOCK</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Dijak</em>&#8220;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">I have finished up with MLW and I am now a Free Agent<br><br>BookDijak@gmail.com <a href="https://t.co/sFtxOBH3mF">pic.twitter.com/sFtxOBH3mF</a></p>&mdash; DONOVAN DIJAK (@DijakFYE) <a href="https://x.com/DijakFYE/status/2119814558709854386?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 9, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397054-former-wwe-talent-confirms-departure-from-mlw/">Former WWE talent confirms departure from MLW</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397054-former-wwe-talent-confirms-departure-from-mlw/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>John Cena reveals new details for the John Cena Classic</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397047-john-cena-reveals-new-details-for-the-john-cena-classic/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397047-john-cena-reveals-new-details-for-the-john-cena-classic/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 19:29:51 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[John Cena]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[John Cena Classic]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397047</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In speaking exclusively to The Takedown on SI, WWE&#8217;s John Cena revealed new details for the John Cena&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397047-john-cena-reveals-new-details-for-the-john-cena-classic/">John Cena reveals new details for the John Cena Classic</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In speaking exclusively to <a href="https://www.si.com/fannation/wrestling/features/john-cena-reveals-new-details-about-the-upcoming-john-cena-classic-exclusive" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">The Takedown on SI</a>, WWE&#8217;s John Cena revealed new details for the John Cena Classic, while clearing up some misconceptions about the event next month.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cena said it will not not feature a bracket-style tournament, as some fans had speculated. It will instead be  centered around a series of exhibition matches, much like how it was determined who is final opponent was for his retirement match last December. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>&#8220;They&#8217;re all gonna be current [main roster stars] versus NXT. It&#8217;s very much like Saturday Night&#8217;s Main Event, and I love that December 14th is the date, because that&#8217;s one year and one day from my last match. And as soon as I retired, on the way home, I was thinking about how I can [stay] involved.&#8221;</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cena also stated in the interview, the Classic idea and concept was taken from other mainstream sporting events. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>&#8220;I wanna try to create [something like] an Arnold Classic. I took a lot from the Arnold Classic. I took a lot from fan appreciation nights. I took a lot from All-Star games, but I wanna create that situation where fans can come to an event they know every year, they know what the situation is, and we&#8217;re in the pilot.&#8221;</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At the time of this writing, Cody Rhodes and Zilla Fatu are first two participants invited to the John Cena Classic.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The John Cena Classic will take place during a second episode of Monday Night Raw on December 14 at the ESPN Wild World Of Sports Complex at Walt Disney World in Orlando, Florida. The first-ever Cena Classic champion will be awarded a belt that is similar to his old WWE spinner championship belt. Those who are WWE Club Members will get to vote on John Cena Classic participants.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397047-john-cena-reveals-new-details-for-the-john-cena-classic/">John Cena reveals new details for the John Cena Classic</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397047-john-cena-reveals-new-details-for-the-john-cena-classic/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>AEW announces Thanksgiving edition of Collision</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397043-aew-announces-thanksgiving-edition-of-collision/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397043-aew-announces-thanksgiving-edition-of-collision/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 07:42:40 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Collision]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Thanksgiving]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397043</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>AEW has announced a special Thanksgiving edition of Collision, set to be taped on 11/25 after the Thanksgiving&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397043-aew-announces-thanksgiving-edition-of-collision/">AEW announces Thanksgiving edition of Collision</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">AEW has announced a special Thanksgiving edition of Collision, set to be taped on 11/25 after the Thanksgiving Eve edition of Dynamite and air the next night on the United States holiday.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The video on social media is narrated by Tony Schiavone and includes appearances from a number of AEW talents, along with a cameo appearance from non-contracted wrestlers Scott Garland (formerly Scotty 2 Hotty), Curry Man, and Glacier.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Aside from the change in night, Collision will air on TNT and HBO Max at 8:00 p.m. Eastern as usual.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The shows will emanate from the LFCU Arena in Omaha, Nebraska.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
https://twitter.com/AEW/status/2119444834364633465
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397043-aew-announces-thanksgiving-edition-of-collision/">AEW announces Thanksgiving edition of Collision</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397043-aew-announces-thanksgiving-edition-of-collision/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>TNA star reveals she was recently in a car accident, &#8220;so blessed to be alive!&#8221;</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397040-tna-reveals-she-was-recently-in-a-car-accident-so-blessed-to-be-alive/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397040-tna-reveals-she-was-recently-in-a-car-accident-so-blessed-to-be-alive/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 00:56:12 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Impact News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Jada Stone]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TNA]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397040</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>TNA talent Jade Stone revealed Sunday on her Instagram Stories that two days ago she was involved in&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397040-tna-reveals-she-was-recently-in-a-car-accident-so-blessed-to-be-alive/">TNA star reveals she was recently in a car accident, &#8220;so blessed to be alive!&#8221;</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA talent Jade Stone revealed Sunday on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/stories/jada.stoneee/?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">her Instagram Stories</a> that two days ago she was involved in a car accident that left her with several injuries. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Stone said she is &#8216;so blessed to be alive.&#8217;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">TNA wrestler Jada Stone met with a car accident recently, wishing her a speedy recovery. <a href="https://t.co/AxczUPXrtz">pic.twitter.com/AxczUPXrtz</a></p>&mdash; Wrestle Sphere (@wrestlesphere0) <a href="https://x.com/wrestlesphere0/status/2119510833097216479?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 8, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397040-tna-reveals-she-was-recently-in-a-car-accident-so-blessed-to-be-alive/">TNA star reveals she was recently in a car accident, &#8220;so blessed to be alive!&#8221;</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397040-tna-reveals-she-was-recently-in-a-car-accident-so-blessed-to-be-alive/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>WWE roster reportedly departed Saudi Arabia before missile attack on Riyadh</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397037-wwe-roster-reportedly-departed-saudi-arabia-before-missile-attack-on-riyadh/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397037-wwe-roster-reportedly-departed-saudi-arabia-before-missile-attack-on-riyadh/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 00:44:09 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[attacks]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Riyadh]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Saudi Arabia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397037</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>PWInsider is reporting the WWE roster landed safely on Sunday in South Carolina, thus not affected by the&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397037-wwe-roster-reportedly-departed-saudi-arabia-before-missile-attack-on-riyadh/">WWE roster reportedly departed Saudi Arabia before missile attack on Riyadh</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.pwinsider.com/index.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">PWInsider</a> is reporting the WWE roster landed safely on Sunday in South Carolina, thus not affected by the <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/loud-booms-heard-saudi-capital-riyadh-after-early-warning-alert-issued-2026-11-08/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">attacks in Riyadh’s financial district</a>, including the Aramco skyscraper, which was damaged on Sunday after attacks done by Yemen’s Houthi rebel group.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Monday&#8217;s Raw takes place from the Bon Secours Wellness Arena in Greenville, South Carolina.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.pwinsider.com/index.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">PWInsider</a> also reported there still may have been some staff in Riyadh helping with the break down of the production. At the time of the report there was no word if anyone associated with WWE still in the country was affected by Sunday’s attacks.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It was also said that a majority the WWE roster actually flew into Bahrain, a neighboring country and then traveled from there by bus into Riyadh. The belief is some talents traveled in a private plane directly in and out of Riyadh.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397037-wwe-roster-reportedly-departed-saudi-arabia-before-missile-attack-on-riyadh/">WWE roster reportedly departed Saudi Arabia before missile attack on Riyadh</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397037-wwe-roster-reportedly-departed-saudi-arabia-before-missile-attack-on-riyadh/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>International Championship Match added to AEW Full Gear PPV</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397024-international-championship-match-added-to-aew-full-gear-ppv/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397024-international-championship-match-added-to-aew-full-gear-ppv/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 04:38:49 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Adam Copeland]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Full Gear]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[International Championship Match]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397024</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Kazuchika Okada defending the AEW International Championship has been added to next Saturday&#8217;s Full Gear pay-per-view. The men&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397024-international-championship-match-added-to-aew-full-gear-ppv/">International Championship Match added to AEW Full Gear PPV</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Kazuchika Okada defending the AEW International Championship has been added to next Saturday&#8217;s Full Gear pay-per-view.  The men competed in Blood and Guts last Wednesday. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back on the October 21 episode of Dynamite, Copeland teamed with Will Ospreay against Kyle Fletcher and Kevin Knight, that saw Okada interfere and then putting the International Championship belt on a turnbuckle which then saw Copeland hit his head on, costing Copeland and Ospreay the match.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Below is the current lineup for Full Gear. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-AEW World Championship Match: Will Ospreay defends against Kyle Fletcher</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-AEW Women’s World Championship Match: Mercedes Mone defends against Marina Shafir</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-AEW World Tag Team Championship Match: Young Bucks (Matt Jackson and Nick Jackson) defends against Mark Davis and Jake Doyle of the Don Callis Family</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-AEW Women’s World Tag Team Championship Match: The Brawling Birds (Jamie Hayter and Alex Windsor) defends against Wrathlander (Kris Statlander and Harley Cameron)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-AEW World Trios Championships Texas Death Match: Hangman Page, Brody King and Bandido defend against Swerve Strickland &amp; The New Level (Kofi and Austin Creed) </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-AEW International Championship Match: Kazuchika Okada defends against Adam Copeland</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Anarchy in the Arena: The Death Riders an The Conglomeration vs. The Cut </p>


<p>AEW Full Gear airs live on pay-per-view on Saturday, November 14 from the Mortgage Matchup Center in Phoenix, Arizona.</p><p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397024-international-championship-match-added-to-aew-full-gear-ppv/">International Championship Match added to AEW Full Gear PPV</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397024-international-championship-match-added-to-aew-full-gear-ppv/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>MLW Saturday Night Superfight Quick Results &#8211; 11/7/26 (New Champion Crowned, Court Bauer teases &#8220;Special Project&#8221; for 2027)</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/397018-mlw-saturday-night-superfight-quick-results-11-7-26-new-champion-crowned-court-bauer-teases-special-project-for-2027/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/397018-mlw-saturday-night-superfight-quick-results-11-7-26-new-champion-crowned-court-bauer-teases-special-project-for-2027/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 04:21:38 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Misc. News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/7 MLW Saturday Superfight Quick Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[MLW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Saturday Superfight]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397018</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Below are the quick results from the MLW Saturday Night Superfight from the sold-out Cicero Stadium in Cicero,&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/397018-mlw-saturday-night-superfight-quick-results-11-7-26-new-champion-crowned-court-bauer-teases-special-project-for-2027/">MLW Saturday Night Superfight Quick Results &#8211; 11/7/26 (New Champion Crowned, Court Bauer teases &#8220;Special Project&#8221; for 2027)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Below are the quick results from the MLW Saturday Night Superfight from the sold-out <a href="https://mlw.com/2026/11/06/saturday-night-superfight-preview/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cicero Stadium</a> in Cicero, Illinois, which streamed live on VEEPS.  MLW Founder Court Bauer also teased a &#8220;special project&#8221; for 2027.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-MLW Tag Team Championships – Street Fight: Good Brothers (Karl Anderson and Doc Gallows) defeated Glasgow Boys On Top (Joe Coffey and Mark Coffey to retain.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Masha Slamovich def. ZAMAYA</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Tessa Blanchard def. Keyra</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-MLW National Openweight Championship: Austin Aries vs. Matt Riddle ended in a 30-minute time limit draw. Aries said he knows everyone wants five more minutes and says know. Riddle knocks him out and takes the title.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Ultimo Guerrero def. Templario and Titan</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Court Bauer thanks everyone attending. He brings out NJPW Chairman Naoki Sugabayashi. Court says MLW, NJPW, and CMLL are working on a big surprise for 2027 before introducing Yota Tsuji.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">MLW <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f91d.png" alt="🤝" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> NJPW<br><br>BIG things are coming!!<br><br>Order now: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f4fa.png" alt="📺" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <a href="https://t.co/BISft0S5FV">https://t.co/BISft0S5FV</a> <a href="https://t.co/QdJgp1eKNT">pic.twitter.com/QdJgp1eKNT</a></p>&mdash; MLW (@MLW) <a href="https://x.com/MLW/status/2119262618515014141?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 8, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Yota Tsuji def. Trevor Lee</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-MLW Championship – Last Man Standing: Josh Bishop def. Killer Kross to become the new champion</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list"></ul>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">THE BLOOD KING’S REIGN IS OVER!<a href="https://x.com/JoshuaBishop_?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">@JoshuaBishop_</a> is the Last Man Standing!<br><br>Replay <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1fa78.png" alt="🩸" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <a href="https://t.co/BISft0S5FV">https://t.co/BISft0S5FV</a> <a href="https://t.co/Da6J5LB5Up">pic.twitter.com/Da6J5LB5Up</a></p>&mdash; MLW (@MLW) <a href="https://x.com/MLW/status/2119275694249386101?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 8, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Source: <a href="https://www.fightful.com/wrestling/mlw-saturday-night-superfight-results-11-7-killer-kross-yota-tsuji-tessa-blanchard-compete/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Fightful</a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/397018-mlw-saturday-night-superfight-quick-results-11-7-26-new-champion-crowned-court-bauer-teases-special-project-for-2027/">MLW Saturday Night Superfight Quick Results &#8211; 11/7/26 (New Champion Crowned, Court Bauer teases &#8220;Special Project&#8221; for 2027)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
